So `ArrayOfM1<ResourceTypeRecord>::sanitize(c, type_base, data_base)` iterates over `count = lenM1 + 1` records, calling `arrayZ[i].sanitize(c, type_base, data_base)` which is `ResourceTypeRecord::sanitize`.

In `ResourceTypeRecord::sanitize`:
```cpp
inline bool sanitize (hb_sanitize_context_t *c,
                      const void *type_base,
                      const void *data_base) const
{
  TRACE_SANITIZE (this);
  return_trace (c->check_struct (this) &&
                resourcesZ.sanitize (c, type_base,
                                     get_resource_count (),
                                     data_base));
}
```

`resourcesZ` is `OffsetTo<UnsizedArrayOf<ResourceRecord>>`. The sanitize with 3 args (base, count, user_data). This calls `StructAtOffset<UnsizedArrayOf<ResourceRecord>>(type_base, *this).sanitize(c, get_resource_count(), data_base)`.

`get_resource_count()` returns `resCountM1 + 1` if tag is sfnt, else 0.

Then `UnsizedArrayOf<ResourceRecord>::sanitize(c, count, data_base)`:
```cpp
inline bool sanitize (hb_sanitize_context_t *c, unsigned int count, const void *base) const
{
  TRACE_SANITIZE (this);
  if (unlikely (!sanitize_shallow (c, count))) return_trace (false);
  for (unsigned int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    if (unlikely (!arrayZ[i].sanitize (c, base)))
      return_trace (false);
  return_trace (true);
}
```

This iterates over `count` ResourceRecords, calling `arrayZ[i].sanitize(c, data_base)` which is `ResourceRecord::sanitize`:
```cpp
inline bool sanitize (hb_sanitize_context_t *c, const void *data_base) const
{
  TRACE_SANITIZE (this);
  return_trace (c->check_struct (this) &&
                offset.sanitize (c, data_base) &&
                get_face (data_base).sanitize (c));
}
```

`offset` is `OffsetTo<LArrayOf<HBUINT8>, HBUINT24, false>`. `offset.sanitize(c, data_base)` calls `StructAtOffset<LArrayOf<HBUINT8>>(data_base, *this).sanitize(c)`.

Let me look at `LArrayOf` sanitize.

